#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ctlhq-reply-lint: check a draft reply against the operator's reply rules before it is sent.

Usage:
  ctlhq-reply-lint [--max-words N] [--max-words-structured N] [--no-next-step] [--allow a,b,c]
                    [--repo DIR] [--previous FILE] [--json] [FILE]
  cat reply.md | ctlhq-reply-lint
  ctlhq-reply-lint --hook          (Claude Code Stop hook; reads the hook JSON on stdin)
  ctlhq-reply-lint --hook-json     (Codex Stop hook; same input, answers {"decision": "block", "reason": ...} on stdout)
  ctlhq-reply-lint --approval [FILE]   (an approval question asked in chat)

Prints one line per finding, "line: rule: fail|warning: message", then "N failures, M warnings".
Exit 1 on any failure, 0 when there are only warnings or nothing, 2 on a usage error.
--json prints the findings as a JSON array of {line, rule, severity, message} on stdout
and the summary line on stderr.

Failures (exit 1), each with the rule it encodes from home/AGENTS.md:
  table-number   a table without a leading number column (unslop rule 34).
                 "Number every list, table row and paragraph that may be discussed later."
  long-dash      a long dash (unslop rule 13). "Do not use em dashes."
  curly-quote    a curly quote (unslop rule 19).
  next-step      no "next step" anywhere, any case (--no-next-step turns it off).
                 "Then 'Next step: <who> <action>'."
  operator-command  a "next step" line asks you or the operator to run, check, install, open,
                 or launch something and the reply has no fenced code block (fail).
  max-words      more than N words outside fenced code: 400, or 600 when the reply holds a
                 table or a list (--max-words N sets both to N; --max-words-structured N the second).
                 "Discussion replies: at most 300 words."
  label-gloss    a project label (S6, N4, D34, 1B: one or two capitals and one or two
                 digits, or a digit and a capital) whose first sentence has no parenthesis gloss.
                 "Gloss a project label at first use in each reply."
  abbreviation   a warning: an all-caps word of 2 to 5 letters whose first sentence has no
                 expansion in parentheses. "Avoid abbreviations or compressed fragments that
                 make the reader guess." The agent judges whether the reader knows the term, so
                 there is no built-in list; --allow skips names. Text
                 inside backticks is never checked.
  double-meaning a result label that can mean two things: pass, passes, passed, passing,
                 qualify, qualifies, qualified. "Avoid labels such as 'pass' when they could
                 mean either..." Write the exact outcome. A warning: "pass" is fine as a verb. (done and fixed: see claim-evidence.)
  step-actor     a numbered item that starts with an action verb (run, open, install, ...)
                 while neither the item nor the line before the list names who acts (you,
                 operator, I, we, main agent, builder, reviewer, agent). "Name who acts." A warning: a numbered
                 record of past steps needs no actor.

Warnings (printed, exit unaffected):
  sentence-length  a sentence over 25 words. "At most 20 words for an instruction, 25 for an explanation."
  numbered-list    a bulleted list of 3 or more items. "Number every list."
  status-line      over 120 words and no line with proposed, implemented, tested, committed,
                   gate, installed, or "Status:". "Give one status line per reply during work."
  vague-pronoun    a paragraph, list item, or table cell that opens with It or They, or with
                   This, That, These, or Those followed by a verb ("This builds"). "Name the
                   thing when words such as 'it' or 'this' could be unclear."
  claim-evidence   "fixed", "done", or "succeeds" with no hash, exit code, or test name on the line.
                   'Never write "fixed", "done", or "succeeds" without the state and the evidence.'
  chatbot-phrase   unslop rule 20; sycophantic-tone: unslop rule 22.
  vague-noun       a noun that names no exact item: thing, things, stuff, something, the
                   issue, the problem, the other one, some files. "Name the thing when words
                   such as 'it' or 'this' could be unclear."

Turn warnings (printed, exit unaffected). They need context beyond the reply: --repo DIR
and --previous FILE, or, under --hook and --hook-json, the hook input's cwd and
transcript_path.
  next-step-open   the reply reports a finished item (a word such as implemented, tested,
                   committed, installed, accepted, merged, finished, completed, done, or a
                   "Status:" line) and ends the turn while `ctlhq-status --next --json --repo
                   DIR` finds a next step and BLOCKED.md has no open row. Quiet when the
                   newest operator message (from the transcript) asks a question, when the
                   reply asks one (a sentence ending in "?", or a "next step" line that hands
                   the step to you or the operator, other than "none from you"), when the
                   "next step" line waits on running work ("still running", "waiting on" or
                   "waiting for" anything but you or the operator, or "when", "once", "after"
                   followed within 60 characters by reports, returns, finishes, completes,
                   lands, exits, or ends), and when DIR has no PLAN.md milestone table.
                   ctlhq-mode: "A finished item never stops the work."
  repeat-reply     this reply and the previous one have the same "next step" line (case and
                   spacing ignored) and this reply adds no new fact: no new fact token (a word
                   with a digit, a path, or backticked code) and fewer than 10 new words of 4
                   or more letters, "next step" lines left out. The previous reply is the last
                   assistant text before the newest operator or system turn of the transcript,
                   read with bin/ctlhq-transcripts; the rule is quiet when an operator message
                   came after the previous reply. The bar of 10 words was measured on 35 reply
                   pairs with the same next step line, from one long Claude Code session:
                   status pings added 0 to 9 new words, replies with news 13 or more. home/AGENTS.md: "During a wait, one line when the wait starts and
                   one when it ends; never a 'still waiting' loop."

--approval checks an approval question asked in chat. It gets every rule above plus:
  approval-first-sentence  fail: the first sentence does not address the operator (you,
                   your, operator). "A decision question starts with what changes for the
                   operator's result in one plain sentence."
  approval-id      fail: a commit hash, a UUID, or an id such as scope_3 or apr-7f3k in the
                   question. "Lead with the decision in plain words, without JSON, hashes,
                   or IDs."
  approval-budget  fail: the first sentence is over 30 words, or a sentence ending in "?" is
                   over 15 words.

A gloss counts when the same sentence holds a parenthesis after the token, or the token
sits inside one: "D34 (the lock-wait defect)" and "the lock-wait defect (D34)" both pass.
--allow a,b,c adds labels or abbreviations that need no gloss (--labels is an alias).

Stop hook: add {"type": "command", "command": "/path/to/bin/ctlhq-reply-lint --hook"} under
hooks.Stop in settings.json. Claude Code passes JSON with last_assistant_message on stdin;
--hook reads it, prints the findings on stderr, and exits 2 on a failure, which blocks the
stop and sends the findings back to the agent (Claude Code ignores exit 1 for blocking).
It exits 0 when stop_hook_active is set, so it fires at most once per reply.
A reply with no failure but a turn warning is sent back once the same way (exit 2, or
"decision": "block" under --hook-json), headed "warning, sent once". Once means once per
operator message: sending one writes <temp folder>/ctlhq-reply-lint/sent/<sha1 of session_id
and the newest operator message's time> (without a transcript the key is the reply text).
While that file exists the turn warnings stay quiet, so a host that does not set
stop_hook_active cannot loop. When the file cannot be written, the turn warnings stay quiet.
Other warnings alone stay quiet under the hooks.
Plain stdin without --hook is read as the reply text itself.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import json
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
UNSLOP = HERE / "ctlhq-unslop"
STATUS = HERE / "ctlhq-status"
TRANSCRIPTS = HERE / "ctlhq-transcripts"
TURN_RULES = ("next-step-open", "repeat-reply")
NEW_WORDS_MIN = 10
FACT_TOKEN = re.compile(r"`[^`\n]+`|\S*\d\S*|\S+/\S+")
CONTENT_WORD = re.compile(r"[a-z][a-z'-]{3,}")
WAITING = re.compile(
    r"\bstill running\b|\bwaiting (?:on|for) (?!you\b|your\b|the operator\b)"
    r"|\b(?:when|once|after)\b[^.\n]{0,60}?\b(?:reports?|returns?|finish(?:es)?|completes?|lands?|exits?|ends?)\b",
    re.IGNORECASE)
FINISHED = re.compile(r"\b(?:implemented|tested|committed|installed|accepted|merged|finished|completed?|done)\b|^\W*status:",
                      re.IGNORECASE | re.MULTILINE)
QUESTION = re.compile(r"\?(?=[\s*_)\"']|$)")
OPERATOR_STEP = re.compile(r"\b(?:you|your|yours|operator)\b", re.IGNORECASE)

UNSLOP_RULES = {
    13: ("long-dash", "fail"),
    19: ("curly-quote", "fail"),
    34: ("table-number", "fail"),
    20: ("chatbot-phrase", "warning"),
    22: ("sycophantic-tone", "warning"),
}
BLOCK_START = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:[-*+]|\d+[.)])\s+")
VAGUE_PRONOUN = re.compile(r"^(?:It|They)\b|^(?:This|That|These|Those)\s+(?:is|are|was|were|does|do|did|has|have|means|makes|runs|builds|covers|keeps|holds|shows|gives|works|needs|lets|adds|says|will|can|would|should|stays|goes|comes|took|takes|fails|failed|passes|checks|reads|writes)\b")
STATUS_WORDS = re.compile(r"\b(?:proposed|implemented|tested|committed|gate|installed)\b|Status:", re.IGNORECASE)
CLAIM = re.compile(r"\b(?:fixed|done|succeeds)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
EVIDENCE = re.compile(
    r"\b(?=[0-9a-f]*\d)(?=[0-9a-f]*[a-f])[0-9a-f]{7,40}\b"  # a commit hash
    r"|\bexit(?: code)?:? ?\d+"  # an exit code
    r"|\btests?/\S+|\b\S+\.sh\b|\btest_\w+|\b\w+_test\b|\b\d+ checks? passed",  # a test name or result
    re.IGNORECASE,
)
LABEL = re.compile(r"\b(?:[A-Z]{1,2}\d{1,2}|\d[A-Z])\b")
ABBREV = re.compile(r"\b[A-Z]{2,5}\b")
NEXT_STEP = re.compile(r"next step", re.IGNORECASE)
FENCE = re.compile(r"^\s*(```|~~~)")
INLINE_CODE = re.compile(r"`[^`\n]*`")
URL = re.compile(r"https?://\S+")
LINK_TARGET = re.compile(r"\]\([^)]*\)")
BULLET = re.compile(r"^(\s*)[-*+]\s+")
NUMBERED = re.compile(r"^\s*\d+[.)]\s+")
HEADING = re.compile(r"^\s*#{1,6}\s")
TABLE_ROW = re.compile(r"^\s*\|.*\|\s*$")
TABLE_SEP = re.compile(r"^\s*\|?\s*:?-{3,}:?\s*(\|\s*:?-{3,}:?\s*)*\|?\s*$")
SENT_END = re.compile(r"(?<=[.!?])\s+")
MAX_SENTENCE = 25
DOUBLE_MEANING = re.compile(r"\b(?:pass(?:es|ed|ing)?|qualif(?:y|ies|ied))\b", re.IGNORECASE)
STEP_VERB = re.compile(
    r"^\s*\d+[.)]\s+(?:\*\*)?(?:run|open|install|click|type|paste|copy|check|add|set|start|restart|stop|"
    r"quit|delete|remove|edit|create|launch|wait|review|approve|merge|commit|push|send|read|write|"
    r"test|update|move|rename|download|upload|enable|disable|sign|load|build|deploy)\b",
    re.IGNORECASE)
ACTOR = re.compile(r"\b(?:you|your|operator|I|we|main agent|builder|reviewer|agent|subagent)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
VAGUE = re.compile(r"\b(?:things?|stuff|something|the issue|the problem|the other one|some files)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
READER = re.compile(r"\b(?:you|your|you'll|you're|operator)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
APPROVAL_ID = re.compile(
    r"\b(?=[0-9a-f]*\d)(?=[0-9a-f]*[a-f])[0-9a-f]{7,40}\b"  # a commit hash
    r"|\b[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\b"  # a UUID
    r"|\b[A-Za-z]+[_-](?=[A-Za-z0-9]*\d)[A-Za-z0-9]+\b",  # an id such as scope_3 or apr-7f3k
    re.IGNORECASE)
QUESTION_MAX = 15
FIRST_SENTENCE_MAX = 30


def usage(msg: str) -> int:
    print(f"ctlhq-reply-lint: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    print("usage: ctlhq-reply-lint [--max-words N] [--max-words-structured N] [--no-next-step] [--allow a,b,c] [--json] [--hook | --approval] [FILE]",
          file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


def hook_input(raw: str) -> dict | None:
    """The reply, cwd, and transcript path from the Stop hook JSON; None means skip (already active or no text)."""
    try:
        o = json.loads(raw)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if not isinstance(o, dict) or o.get("stop_hook_active"):
        return None
    text = hook_text(o)
    if text is None:
        return None
    cwd = o.get("cwd") if isinstance(o.get("cwd"), str) else None
    path = o.get("transcript_path") if isinstance(o.get("transcript_path"), str) else None
    session = o.get("session_id") if isinstance(o.get("session_id"), str) else (path or "")
    return {"reply": text, "cwd": cwd, "transcript": path, "session": session}


def hook_text(o: dict) -> str | None:
    """last_assistant_message, else the last assistant text block in the transcript."""
    m = o.get("last_assistant_message")
    if isinstance(m, str) and m.strip():
        return m
    text = ""
    path = o.get("transcript_path")
    if path:
        try:
            for line in open(path, errors="replace"):
                try:
                    e = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if not isinstance(e, dict) or e.get("type") != "assistant":
                    continue
                for b in (e.get("message") or {}).get("content") or []:
                    if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get("type") == "text" and b.get("text", "").strip():
                        text = b["text"]
        except OSError:
            pass
    return text or None


def unslop_findings(text: str) -> list[tuple[int, str, str, str]]:
    rules = ",".join(str(r) for r in sorted(UNSLOP_RULES))
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(UNSLOP), "--rules", rules], input=text,
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return [(0, "unslop", "fail", f"could not run {UNSLOP}: {e}")]
    if r.returncode not in (0, 1):
        return [(0, "unslop", "fail", f"ctlhq-unslop exited {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:200]}")]
    out = []
    for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"^<stdin>:(\d+): rule (\d+) ([^:]+): (.*)$", line)
        if not m:
            continue
        num = int(m.group(2))
        name, sev = UNSLOP_RULES.get(num, (f"unslop-{num}", "fail"))
        out.append((int(m.group(1)), name, sev, f"unslop rule {num} {m.group(3)}: {m.group(4)}"))
    return out


def prose_lines(lines: list[str]) -> tuple[list[str], set[str]]:
    """Lines with fenced code blanked and inline code, URLs, link targets masked; plus backticked tokens."""
    out, ticked, in_fence = [], set(), False
    for ln in lines:
        if FENCE.match(ln):
            in_fence = not in_fence
            out.append("")
            continue
        if in_fence:
            out.append("")
            continue
        for m in INLINE_CODE.finditer(ln):
            ticked.update(re.findall(r"\w+", m.group(0)))
        ln = INLINE_CODE.sub("code", ln)
        ln = LINK_TARGET.sub("]", ln)
        ln = URL.sub("link", ln)
        out.append(ln)
    return out, ticked


def blocks(lines: list[str]) -> list[list[tuple[int, str]]]:
    """Group prose lines into paragraphs, list items, headings, and table rows: [(line number, text)]."""
    out: list[list[tuple[int, str]]] = []
    cur: list[tuple[int, str]] | None = None
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not ln.strip() or TABLE_SEP.match(ln):
            cur = None
            continue
        if TABLE_ROW.match(ln) or HEADING.match(ln):
            out.append([(i, ln)])
            cur = None
            continue
        if BULLET.match(ln) or NUMBERED.match(ln) or cur is None:
            cur = [(i, ln)]
            out.append(cur)
        else:
            cur.append((i, ln))
    return out


def sentences(block: list[tuple[int, str]]) -> list[tuple[int, str]]:
    """Split a block into sentences; each carries the line number where it starts."""
    text, starts = "", []
    for n, ln in block:
        ln = BULLET.sub("", NUMBERED.sub("", HEADING.sub("", ln)))
        if TABLE_ROW.match(ln):
            ln = ln.replace("|", " ")
        starts.append((len(text), n))
        text += ln.strip() + " "
    out, pos = [], 0
    for part in SENT_END.split(text):
        idx = text.find(part, pos)
        pos = idx + len(part)
        if not part.strip():
            continue
        line = max((n for off, n in starts if off <= idx), default=block[0][0])
        out.append((line, part.strip()))
    return out


def glossed(sentence: str, start: int, end: int) -> bool:
    """True when a parenthesis follows the token in this sentence, or the token sits inside one."""
    if "(" in sentence[end:]:
        return True
    before = sentence[:start]
    return before.rfind("(") > before.rfind(")")


NOTHING_FROM_YOU = re.compile(r"\b(?:none|nothing)(?: needed)? from (?:you|the operator)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
OPERATOR_ACTION = re.compile(r"\b(?:you|operator)\b.{0,40}\b(?:run|runs|execute|install|check|test|restart|start|open|paste|type|launch|verify)\b", re.IGNORECASE)
TABLE_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s*\|.*\|\s*$")
LIST_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:[-*+]|\d+[.)])\s+\S")


def prose_lines_for_budget(text: str) -> list:
    out, fence = [], False
    for ln in text.split("\n"):
        if ln.lstrip().startswith("```"):
            fence = not fence
            continue
        if not fence:
            out.append(ln)
    return out


def lint(text: str, max_words: int, need_next: bool, allow: set[str], max_structured: int = 600) -> list[tuple[int, str, str, str]]:
    raw = text.split("\n")
    lines, ticked = prose_lines(raw)
    findings = unslop_findings(text)

    words, in_fence = 0, False  # every word outside fenced code counts, inline code included
    for r in raw:
        if FENCE.match(r):
            in_fence = not in_fence
        elif not in_fence:
            words += len(r.split())
    if need_next and not any(NEXT_STEP.search(ln) for ln in lines):
        findings.append((len(raw), "next-step", "fail", "no 'Next step' line; add 'Next step: <who> <action>'"))
    has_fence = any(FENCE.match(r) for r in raw)
    for n, ln in enumerate(raw, 1):
        if NEXT_STEP.search(ln) and OPERATOR_ACTION.search(ln) and not NOTHING_FROM_YOU.search(ln) and not has_fence:
            findings.append((n, "operator-command", "fail", "the next step asks the operator to run or check something; put the exact command in a code block in this reply"))
            break
    structured = any(TABLE_LINE.match(ln) or LIST_LINE.match(ln) for ln in prose_lines_for_budget(text))
    limit = max_structured if (structured and max_structured) else max_words
    if words > limit:
        findings.append((1, "max-words", "fail", f"{words} words outside code blocks (limit {limit}{', table or list present' if limit != max_words else ''}); "
                                                 "shorten it or move detail to a file"))

    seen_label, seen_abbrev = set(), set()
    for blk in blocks(lines):
        is_table = TABLE_ROW.match(blk[0][1]) is not None
        is_heading = HEADING.match(blk[0][1]) is not None
        for n, s in sentences(blk):
            for m in LABEL.finditer(s):
                tok = m.group(0)
                if tok in seen_label or tok in allow or tok in ticked:
                    continue
                seen_label.add(tok)
                if not glossed(s, m.start(), m.end()):
                    findings.append((n, "label-gloss", "fail",
                                     f"{tok} has no gloss on first use; write '{tok} (what it is)'"))
            for m in ABBREV.finditer(s):
                tok = m.group(0)
                if tok in seen_abbrev or tok in allow or tok in ticked:
                    continue
                seen_abbrev.add(tok)
                if not glossed(s, m.start(), m.end()):
                    findings.append((n, "abbreviation", "warning",
                                     f"{tok} is not expanded on first use; write the words with '({tok})' "
                                     "or pass --allow"))
            if not is_table and not is_heading:
                count = len(s.split())
                if count > MAX_SENTENCE:
                    findings.append((n, "sentence-length", "warning",
                                     f"sentence of {count} words (limit {MAX_SENTENCE}); split it"))

    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not ln.strip() or HEADING.match(ln):
            continue
        if TABLE_ROW.match(ln):
            starts = ln.strip().strip("|").split("|")
        elif BLOCK_START.match(ln) or i == 1 or not lines[i - 2].strip():
            starts = [ln]
        else:
            continue
        for cell in starts:
            m = VAGUE_PRONOUN.match(BLOCK_START.sub("", cell.strip(), count=1).lstrip("*_ "))
            if m:
                findings.append((i, "vague-pronoun", "warning",
                                 f"'{m.group(0).strip()}' opens a block; name the thing it points to"))
    run_start, run_len, run_indent = 0, 0, None
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines + [""], 1):
        m = BULLET.match(ln)
        if m and (run_indent is None or len(m.group(1)) == run_indent):
            if run_len == 0:
                run_start, run_indent = i, len(m.group(1))
            run_len += 1
            continue
        if m or (ln.startswith((" ", "\t")) and ln.strip() and run_len):
            continue  # a nested item or a wrapped line inside the run
        if run_len >= 3:
            findings.append((run_start, "numbered-list", "warning",
                             f"bulleted list of {run_len} items; consider numbering it"))
        run_start, run_len, run_indent = 0, 0, None

    if words > 120 and not any(STATUS_WORDS.search(ln) for ln in lines):
        findings.append((1, "status-line", "warning",
                         "no status line (proposed, implemented, tested, committed, gate, installed, or 'Status:')"))

    for i, (ln, r) in enumerate(zip(lines, raw), 1):
        m = CLAIM.search(ln)
        if m and not EVIDENCE.search(r):
            findings.append((i, "claim-evidence", "warning",
                             f"'{m.group(0)}' with no hash, exit code, or test name on the line"))

    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
        m = DOUBLE_MEANING.search(ln)
        if m:
            findings.append((i, "double-meaning", "warning",
                             f"'{m.group(0)}' can mean two things; write the exact outcome (the test ran and exited 0, the OS blocked it)"))
        m = VAGUE.search(ln)
        if m:
            findings.append((i, "vague-noun", "warning", f"'{m.group(0)}' names no exact item; name the file, test, or step"))

    lead = ""
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
        if not NUMBERED.match(ln):
            if ln.strip() and not ln.startswith((" ", "\t")):
                lead = ln
            continue
        if STEP_VERB.match(ln) and not ACTOR.search(ln) and not ACTOR.search(lead):
            findings.append((i, "step-actor", "warning", "a numbered step with no actor; say who does it (you, the main agent, the builder)"))

    return sorted(set(findings), key=lambda f: (f[0], f[1], f[3]))  # one row per line, rule, and message


def next_step_index(lines: list[str]) -> int:
    """The 1-based number of the last line that holds "next step", or 0."""
    return max((i for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if NEXT_STEP.search(ln)), default=0)


def next_step_line(lines: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """The last line that holds "next step", lowercased with markup and spacing removed."""
    i = next_step_index(lines)
    return " ".join(re.sub(r"[*_`]", "", lines[i - 1]).lower().split()) if i else None


def asks_question(lines: list[str]) -> bool:
    if any(QUESTION.search(ln) for ln in lines):
        return True
    i = next_step_index(lines)
    step = lines[i - 1] if i else ""
    return bool(OPERATOR_STEP.search(step)) and not NOTHING_FROM_YOU.search(step)


def plan_next(repo: str) -> dict | None:
    """ctlhq-status --next --json for repo, or None when it does not answer."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(STATUS), "--next", "--json", "--repo", repo],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=2)
        return json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        return None


def next_step_open(text: str, repo: str, operator: str | None) -> list[tuple[int, str, str, str]]:
    lines, _ = prose_lines(text.split("\n"))
    i = next_step_index(lines)
    if not FINISHED.search("\n".join(lines)) or (operator is not None and QUESTION.search(operator)):
        return []
    if asks_question(lines) or (i and WAITING.search(lines[i - 1])):
        return []
    nx = plan_next(repo)
    if not nx or not nx.get("step") or nx.get("blocked_open"):
        return []
    s = nx["step"]
    return [(i, "next-step-open", "warning",
             f"this reply reports a finished item, PLAN.md line {s.get('line')} has a next step ({s.get('milestone')}, "
             f"{s.get('state')}), BLOCKED.md has no open row, and the reply asks no question; a finished item never "
             "stops the work: start that step, or say which decision the operator kept, or which blocker, stops you")]


def fact_tokens(lines: list[str]) -> set[str]:
    out = set()
    for ln in lines:
        for m in FACT_TOKEN.finditer(ln):
            tok = re.sub(r"'s$", "", m.group(0).strip(".,;:()[]{}\"'*_!?")).lower()
            if tok:
                out.add(tok)
    return out


def content_words(lines: list[str]) -> set[str]:
    return {re.sub(r"'s$", "", w) for ln in lines for w in CONTENT_WORD.findall(ln.lower())}


def repeat_reply(text: str, previous: str) -> list[tuple[int, str, str, str]]:
    raw_now, raw_before = text.split("\n"), previous.split("\n")
    step_now, step_before = next_step_line(raw_now), next_step_line(raw_before)
    if step_now is None or step_now != step_before:
        return []
    body_now = [ln for ln in raw_now if not NEXT_STEP.search(ln)]
    body_before = [ln for ln in raw_before if not NEXT_STEP.search(ln)]
    new_facts = fact_tokens(body_now) - fact_tokens(body_before)
    new_words = content_words(body_now) - content_words(body_before)
    if new_facts or len(new_words) >= NEW_WORDS_MIN:
        return []
    return [(next_step_index(raw_now), "repeat-reply", "warning",
             f"same next step line as the previous reply and no new fact ({len(new_words)} new words, no new number, path, or code); "
             "during a wait, write one line when it starts and one when it ends, and stop without another status reply")]


def transcript_context(transcript: str) -> dict:
    """From ctlhq-transcripts: the previous reply (None when the operator wrote since it), the newest
    operator message, and that message's time."""
    out: dict = {"previous": None, "operator": None, "operator_ts": None}
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(TRANSCRIPTS), "turns", transcript, "--role", "all", "--text-only", "--json"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=2)
        turns = json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else []
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        return out
    turns = [t for t in turns if isinstance(t, dict)] if isinstance(turns, list) else []
    op = max((i for i, t in enumerate(turns) if t.get("role") == "operator"), default=None)
    if op is not None:
        out["operator"], out["operator_ts"] = turns[op].get("text") or "", turns[op].get("ts")
    last_other = max((i for i, t in enumerate(turns) if t.get("role") != "assistant"), default=None)
    if last_other is None:
        return out
    prev = max((i for i in range(last_other) if turns[i].get("role") == "assistant" and (turns[i].get("text") or "").strip()),
               default=None)
    if prev is not None and (op is None or op < prev):
        out["previous"] = turns[prev]["text"]
    return out


def sent_marker(session: str, key: str) -> Path:
    """The once-file for a turn warning, under the temp folder, so no project gets untracked files."""
    base = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / "ctlhq-reply-lint" / "sent"
    return base / hashlib.sha1(f"{session}\n{key}".encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def turn_findings(text: str, repo: str | None, previous: str | None, operator: str | None = None) -> list[tuple[int, str, str, str]]:
    out = []
    if repo:
        out += next_step_open(text, repo, operator)
    if previous is not None:
        out += repeat_reply(text, previous)
    return out


def words_in(text: str) -> int:
    return len(text.split())


def first_sentence(text: str) -> str:
    """The first prose sentence, headings and code skipped."""
    body = " ".join(l.strip() for l in prose_lines(text.split("\n"))[0] if l.strip() and not HEADING.match(l))
    parts = [p for p in SENT_END.split(body) if p.strip()]
    return parts[0] if parts else ""


def lint_approval_text(text: str) -> list:
    out = []
    first = first_sentence(text)
    if not READER.search(first):
        out.append((1, "approval-first-sentence", "fail",
                    "the first sentence must say what you (the operator) will see or get; start with that"))
    if words_in(first) > FIRST_SENTENCE_MAX:
        out.append((1, "approval-budget", "fail", f"first sentence of {words_in(first)} words (limit {FIRST_SENTENCE_MAX})"))
    lines, _ = prose_lines(text.split("\n"))
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
        for m in APPROVAL_ID.finditer(ln):
            out.append((i, "approval-id", "fail", f"'{m.group(0)}' is a hash or id; say in plain words what it stands for"))
        for q in SENT_END.split(ln):
            q = NUMBERED.sub("", BULLET.sub("", q)).strip()
            if q.endswith("?") and words_in(q) > QUESTION_MAX:
                out.append((i, "approval-budget", "fail", f"question of {words_in(q)} words (limit {QUESTION_MAX})"))
    return out


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    max_words, need_next, as_json, hook, approval = 400, True, False, False, False
    hook_json = False
    max_structured = 600
    repo: str | None = None
    previous_file: str | None = None
    allow: set[str] = set()
    files: list[str] = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__.strip())
            return 0
        if a == "--max-words":
            i += 1
            if i >= len(argv) or not argv[i].isdigit():
                return usage("--max-words needs a whole number")
            max_words = int(argv[i])
            max_structured = max_words
        elif a in ("--allow", "--labels"):
            i += 1
            if i >= len(argv):
                return usage(f"{a} needs a list like S6,MCP")
            allow.update(x.strip() for x in argv[i].split(",") if x.strip())
        elif a == "--max-words-structured":
            i += 1
            if i >= len(argv) or not argv[i].isdigit():
                return usage("--max-words-structured needs a whole number")
            max_structured = int(argv[i])
        elif a in ("--repo", "--previous"):
            i += 1
            if i >= len(argv):
                return usage(f"{a} needs a value")
            if a == "--repo":
                repo = argv[i]
            else:
                previous_file = argv[i]
        elif a == "--no-next-step":
            need_next = False
        elif a == "--json":
            as_json = True
        elif a == "--hook":
            hook = True
        elif a == "--hook-json":
            hook = True
            hook_json = True
        elif a == "--approval":
            approval = True
        elif a.startswith("-") and a != "-":
            return usage(f"unknown option {a}")
        else:
            files.append(a)
        i += 1
    if len(files) > 1:
        return usage("give one FILE, or none to read stdin")
    if hook and files:
        return usage("--hook reads stdin; drop the FILE")
    if hook and approval:
        return usage("--approval and --hook do not combine")
    if hook and (repo or previous_file):
        return usage("--hook reads cwd and transcript_path from its input; drop --repo and --previous")
    previous: str | None = None
    operator: str | None = None
    once_key: str | None = None
    marker: Path | None = None
    if previous_file is not None:
        try:
            previous = Path(previous_file).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
            return usage(f"cannot read --previous {previous_file} ({e})")

    if files and files[0] != "-":
        try:
            text = Path(files[0]).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
            return usage(f"cannot read {files[0]} ({e})")
    else:
        text = sys.stdin.read()
    if hook:
        got = hook_input(text)
        if got is None:
            if hook_json:
                print(json.dumps({"continue": True}))
            return 0
        text = got["reply"]
        repo = got["cwd"]
        if got["transcript"]:
            ctx = transcript_context(got["transcript"])
            previous, operator = ctx["previous"], ctx["operator"]
            once_key = f"operator turn {ctx['operator_ts']}" if ctx["operator_ts"] else once_key
        marker = sent_marker(got["session"], once_key or f"reply {text}")

    extra = lint_approval_text(text) if approval else turn_findings(text, repo, previous, operator)
    findings = sorted(set(lint(text, max_words, need_next, allow, max_structured) + extra), key=lambda f: (f[0], f[1], f[3]))
    fails = sum(1 for f in findings if f[2] == "fail")
    warns = len(findings) - fails
    summary = f"{fails} failures, {warns} warnings"
    if hook:
        turn = [f for f in findings if f[1] in TURN_RULES]
        if turn and marker is not None and marker.exists():
            findings = [f for f in findings if f[1] not in TURN_RULES]
            turn = []
            fails = sum(1 for f in findings if f[2] == "fail")
            summary = f"{fails} failures, {len(findings) - fails} warnings"
        if fails:
            lines = ["Reply check (ctlhq-reply-lint): fix these before you stop."]
            shown = findings
        elif turn:
            lines = ["Reply check (ctlhq-reply-lint): warning, sent once. Continue the work, or stop again."]
            shown = turn
        else:
            lines, shown = [], []
        if turn and marker is not None:
            try:
                marker.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                marker.write_text(summary + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
            except OSError:
                shown = [f for f in shown if f[1] not in TURN_RULES]
                if not fails:
                    lines, shown = [], []
        lines += [f"{n}: {rule}: {sev}: {msg}" for n, rule, sev, msg in shown]
        if shown:
            lines.append(summary)
        if hook_json:
            print(json.dumps({"decision": "block", "reason": "\n".join(lines)}) if shown else json.dumps({"continue": True}))
            return 0
        if shown:
            print("\n".join(lines), file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return 0
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps([{"line": n, "rule": rule, "severity": sev, "message": msg}
                          for n, rule, sev, msg in findings], indent=2))
        print(summary, file=sys.stderr)
    else:
        for n, rule, sev, msg in findings:
            print(f"{n}: {rule}: {sev}: {msg}")
        print(summary)
    return 1 if fails else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
